Workstream ID: atlas-unseen-level-ups
Title: Automatically present unseen Atlas level-ups on arrival
Status: IN_REVIEW
Milestone: Celebrate every newly earned chapter on the next Atlas visit
Dependencies: discovery-atlas, atlas-progression-redesign, atlas-living-motion
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/CareerOS/issues/33
Purpose: Automatically play each earned but unseen Wayfinder level-up in order
  when the user returns to Discovery Atlas, including gains made on other pages
  or before a reload. Remember presentation separately from real progress.

Tasks:
  [x] Trace existing notification, timeline, source and tutorial boundaries.
  [x] Track seen chapter presentation without changing workspace/backup formats.
  [x] Start after the visible renderer or explicit fallback is ready.
  [x] Preserve every crossed level, interruptions, replay, skip and reduced motion.
  [x] Qualify persistence, source replacement, errors and tutorial isolation.
  [x] Update focused documentation, original tracking and owned continuity.

Acceptance criteria:
  The first Atlas arrival automatically presents all unseen crossed thresholds
    in ascending order, not only the latest or a clicked notification.
  Already presented chapters do not automatically repeat after route changes
    or reloads; interrupted playback retains later unseen chapters.
  Loading or hidden/offscreen time cannot consume automatic ceremonies.
    Explicit skip/dismiss and authoritative reduced motion remain available.
  A small browser-local presentation preference is not EXP, a progress writer,
    a backup/journal field or a second reward ledger. Errors are visible.
  Tutorial practice neither reads nor writes the personal presentation marker.
    Source replacement cannot turn an old sequence into unearned rewards.
  Existing replay, unearned preview, actual records, criteria and rendering
    budgets remain intact. Preserve the preceding local README/media work.
  This is a local review candidate, not new Git publication or human approval.

